    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:opsz,wght@9..40,400;9..40,500;9..40,600;9..40,700&family=DM+Serif+Display:ital@0;1&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#content">Skip to main content</a>
    <header class="site-header english-header" data-header><a class="brand" href="#home" aria-label="Back to the guide"><svg class="brand-mark" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 43h40M19 40l8-15h10l8 15M23 43a6 6 0 1 1 0 12 6 6 0 0 1 0-12Zm18 0a6 6 0 1 1 0 12 6 6 0 0 1 0-12Z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M27 25 22 17h9l6 8" fill="none" stroke="#B7472A" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span><strong>Fatahillah</strong><small>Kota Tua Guide</small></span></a><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="#choose">Choose</a><a href="#square">Square</a><a href="#museum">Museum</a><a href="#maps">Maps</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></nav><div class="header-actions"><a class="language-switch" href="/" lang="id">ID</a><a class="header-cta" href="#choose">Plan a visit <span>↘</span></a></div></header>
    <main id="content"><section id="home" class="hero"><div class="hero-photo" style={`background-image:linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(9,35,31,.9),rgba(9,35,31,.55),rgba(9,35,31,.16)),url(${museumImage});`}></div><div class="hero-route"></div><div class="hero-stamp"><span>Kota Tua</span><b>Jakarta</b><i>•</i><span>Visitor Guide</span></div><div class="hero-content"><p class="eyebrow light">Kota Tua · Jakarta, Indonesia</p><h1>Two places,<br /><em>one old town.</em></h1><p class="hero-lede">An independent field guide to the open square of Taman Fatahillah and the indoor story of Jakarta History Museum.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href="#choose">Choose a place <span>→</span></a><a class="text-link light" href="#maps">Open both maps <span>↓</span></a></div></div><div class="hero-meta"><span>01 / KOTA TUA</span><span>-6.135, 106.811</span></div></section>
      <section id="choose" class="section place-selector-section"><div class="route-number">01 <span>/ CHOOSE YOUR VISIT</span></div><div class="selector-heading"><h2>Two settings,<br /><em>two different rhythms.</em></h2><p>The square and the museum sit opposite each other, but they are not the same visit. One is a free outdoor civic space; the other is a ticketed indoor museum with fixed opening hours.</p></div><div class="place-selector-grid"><article class="place-card"><img src={squareImage} alt="Taman Fatahillah and historic Kota Tua façades" loading="lazy" /><div class="place-card-body"><p class="eyebrow">01 / OUTDOOR</p><h3>Taman Fatahillah</h3><p>A public stone square for walking, colourful ontel bicycles, street culture and Kota Tua façades.</p><div><a class="text-link" href="#square">Read square guide <span>→</span></a><a class="map-mini-link" href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/5h3gQRZc4fwgGoU97" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open square map ↗</a></div></div></article><article class="place-card museum-card"><img src={museumImage} alt="Jakarta History Museum, the former Batavia City Hall" loading="lazy" /><div class="place-card-body"><p class="eyebrow">02 / INDOOR</p><h3>Jakarta History Museum</h3><p>Jakarta’s history in a former city hall: collections, maps, a courtroom and underground cells.</p><div><a class="text-link" href="#museum">Read museum guide <span>→</span></a><a class="map-mini-link" href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/XaSitKkU9B9Wd5Lf6" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open museum map ↗</a></div></div></article></div></section>
      <section id="square" class="section intro-section"><div class="route-number">02 <span>/ TAMAN FATAHILLAH</span></div><div class="intro-layout"><h2>The square as<br /><em>a living room.</em></h2><div class="copy-block"><p>Taman Fatahillah is the former <i>Stadhuisplein</i>, the civic square in front of Batavia’s City Hall. It is now a public meeting point where old-town architecture, informal activity, cultural events and everyday movement share the same paving.</p><p>The square is generally open at all hours and does not have an entry ticket. Morning and late afternoon are often easier for walking; bicycle rentals and street activity are usually concentrated in daylight hours.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/5h3gQRZc4fwgGoU97" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open Taman Fatahillah in Maps <span>↗</span></a></div></div><div class="facts-strip"><article><span class="fact-symbol">◎</span><p>ACCESS</p><h3>Public square</h3><small>Outdoor civic space in Kota Tua.</small></article><article><span class="fact-symbol">↻</span><p>ENTRY</p><h3>No general ticket</h3><small>Separate activities may have their own terms.</small></article><article><span class="fact-symbol">◷</span><p>TIME</p><h3>24 hours</h3><small>Daylight is best for most activity.</small></article><article><span class="fact-symbol">◌</span><p>STAY</p><h3>45–90 minutes</h3><small>Allow longer if combining nearby museums.</small></article></div></section>
      <section id="museum" class="section museum-section"><div class="route-number">03 <span>/ JAKARTA HISTORY MUSEUM</span></div><div class="museum-layout"><div><p class="eyebrow">FORMER BATAVIA CITY HALL</p><h2>Read Jakarta<br /><em>from the inside.</em></h2><p>The museum occupies the former <i>Stadhuis van Batavia</i>. Its visit is intentionally different from the open square: allow time for historical collections, city maps, period furniture, the courtroom and underground cells.</p><p>It is a ticketed indoor attraction. Reference information lists Tuesday–Friday, 09:00–15:00 WIB; Saturday–Sunday, 09:00–20:00 WIB; Monday closed. Always check current details before travelling.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/XaSitKkU9B9Wd5Lf6" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open the museum in Maps <span>↗</span></a></div><aside class="museum-note"><p>REFERENCE HOURS</p><strong>Tue–Fri<br />09:00–15:00</strong><strong>Sat–Sun<br />09:00–20:00</strong><strong>Monday<br />Closed</strong><small>Opening arrangements can change; verify before departure.</small></aside></div><div class="museum-info-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Tickets</h3><p>Indonesia Travel lists reference prices of Rp15,000 for adult Indonesian visitors, Rp5,000 for students, and Rp50,000 for foreign visitors. Confirm locally before you go.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Suggested stay</h3><p>Allow 60–120 minutes for the main galleries, courtroom and underground cells. Start near opening time for an unhurried indoor visit.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Getting there</h3><p>Use the museum pin, not only the square name, for taxis and ride-hailing. Parking, toilets and food options follow wider Kota Tua arrangements.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>What to notice</h3><p>Look for the building’s civic architecture and for the narrative from Sunda Kelapa and Jayakarta to colonial Batavia and modern Jakarta.</p></article></div></section>
      <section id="maps" class="section map-section"><div class="route-number light">04 <span>/ TWO MAPS</span></div><div class="map-heading"><div><h2>Choose the right<br /><em>destination pin.</em></h2><p>The two destinations are adjacent but distinct. Use the appropriate map for the type of visit you have planned.</p></div></div><div class="map-grid"><article class="map-card"><div class="map-card-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / SQUARE</p><h3>Taman Fatahillah</h3><p>Jl. Lada Dalam No.7, Pinangsia.</p></div><a class="button coral" href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/5h3gQRZc4fwgGoU97" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open map <span>↗</span></a></div><div class="map-frame"><iframe title="Taman Fatahillah map" src="https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d6854.384557396718!2d106.81070202690715!3d-6.134920560150956!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x2e6a1dff3f8f5fed%3A0xf2536e698fceab32!2sTaman%20Fatahillah!5e1!3m2!1sen!2sid!4v1787021134348!5m2!1sen!2sid" width="600" height="450" style="border:0" allowfullscreen loading="lazy"></iframe></div></article><article class="map-card"><div class="map-card-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / MUSEUM</p><h3>Jakarta History Museum</h3><p>Taman Fatahillah No.1, Pinangsia.</p></div><a class="button coral" href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/XaSitKkU9B9Wd5Lf6" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open map <span>↗</span></a></div><div class="map-frame"><iframe title="Jakarta History Museum map" src="https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d6854.3812539333985!2d106.81077487690717!3d-6.135177460153231!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x2e6a1dff4292a57d%3A0x12f0032d678c0745!2sJakarta%20History%20Museum!5e1!3m2!1sen!2sid!4v1787020766802!5m2!1sen!2sid" width="600" height="450" style="border:0" allowfullscreen loading="lazy"></iframe></div></article></div></section>
      <section id="faq" class="section faq-section"><div class="route-number">05 <span>/ FAQ</span></div><div class="faq-heading"><h2>Before you<br /><em>set off.</em></h2><p>These answers are starting points only. Check official channels for current access, events and service details shortly before your visit.</p></div><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Is Taman Fatahillah free to enter?<span>+</span></summary><p>The square is generally accessible as a public space without an entry ticket. Individual activities may set their own terms.</p></details><details><summary>Does Jakarta History Museum require a ticket?<span>+</span></summary><p>Yes. It is a ticketed museum with separate opening hours. Confirm the latest price and timetable before visiting.</p></details><details><summary>How do I get there from the airport?<span>+</span></summary><p>Consider an official taxi, hired car, or ride-hailing to Kota Tua. For public transport, check current rail and connecting-service routes before travelling.</p></details><details><summary>Are parking, toilets and food available?<span>+</span></summary><p>Availability changes with Kota Tua management and events. Use official parking, verify facilities on arrival, and choose food or convenience categories based on your needs.</p></details></div></section>
    </main>
